WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:12.083
Your software library stores a release once so you can deploy
the same version to different devices later. Publishing alone
does not install it. Choose Components in the sidebar to publish
software.

2
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.213
Name the component and give the release a semantic version.

3
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.189
Choose the platform and attach the artifact for it.

4
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:28.253
Delivery: choose Confidential for proprietary software. This
public demo artifact is published unencrypted.

5
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.717
Review, then upload to Walrus and register the version. Approve
the transaction.

6
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.973
Version published. It is now in the library, ready to deploy.

